course: dictionary
lesson: 13591
title: Squashing things: incompressible
level: primary-4
stars: 0
explain: Some things can be squashed into a smaller space, and some cannot. Incompressible means not able to be squashed into a smaller space. The start in- means not, and compress means to press together, so incompressible means "not able to be pressed together".
explain: Try it with a syringe. «Push the plunger on a syringe full of air and it squashes easily.» Air is compressible. Now try a syringe full of water: «Push the plunger on a syringe full of water and it hardly moves.» Water is almost incompressible.
explain: Why does this happen? In a gas, the tiny particles are far apart, so there is space to squash them together. In a liquid or a solid, the particles are already close together, so there is hardly any room to squeeze them. Check your idea: swap "incompressible" into the sentence and see if it still makes sense.
fact: Incompressible means not able to be squashed into a smaller space.
fact: «The water in the syringe is almost incompressible.» Its volume stays nearly the same when you press on it.
fact: Liquids and solids are almost incompressible, because their particles are already close together.
fact: Gases are compressible: «Air in a syringe squashes easily.»
fact: Hydraulic machines use liquids because liquids are almost incompressible.
exercise: «Air in a syringe squashes easily.» Is air compressible or incompressible? | Incompressible | Heavy | *Compressible | Solid
exercise: What does incompressible mean? | Made of metal | Very hot | *Not able to be squashed into a smaller space | Able to be squashed very small
exercise: Which of these is almost incompressible? | Air | A balloon full of air | *Water | A sponge
test: Why are liquids almost incompressible? | *Their particles are already close together | Their particles are far apart | They have no particles at all | They are always hot
test: «The mechanic used a hydraulic machine filled with oil.» Why does a hydraulic machine use a liquid? | *Because liquids are almost incompressible | Because liquids are lighter than air | Because liquids can be squashed very small | Because liquids are always cold
exam: Which sentence describes an incompressible substance? | «The balloon shrank as the gas leaked out.» | «The air in the bag squashed flat.» | *«When I pressed the full water bottle, it hardly changed size.» | «The sponge got smaller when I squeezed it.»
